{"files":[{"content":"/*\n  Quicksort\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <openssl/md5.h>\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\n/*\n * Prototypes\n */\nvoid srandnum(int seed);\ndouble randnum(void);\nint *generate_case(int N);\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax);\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j);\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N);\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N);\n\n#define RADIX_BASE 256u\n#define RADIX_PARALLEL_MIN 32768u\n\nstatic unsigned int radix_key(int value)\n{\n    return (unsigned int)value ^ (UINT_MAX - (UINT_MAX >> 1));\n}\n\nstatic void radix_sort_serial(int *values, int *buffer, size_t count)\n{\n    int *source = values;\n    int *target = buffer;\n\n    for (unsigned int shift = 0;\n         shift < sizeof(unsigned int) * CHAR_BIT;\n         shift += 8) {\n        size_t offsets[RADIX_BASE] = {0};\n\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n            unsigned int bucket = (radix_key(source[i]) >> shift) & 0xffu;\n            offsets[bucket]++;\n        }\n\n        size_t prefix = 0;\n        for (unsigned int bucket = 0; bucket < RADIX_BASE; bucket++) {\n            size_t bucket_count = offsets[bucket];\n            offsets[bucket] = prefix;\n            prefix += bucket_count;\n        }\n\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n            unsigned int bucket = (radix_key(source[i]) >> shift) & 0xffu;\n            target[offsets[bucket]++] = source[i];\n        }\n\n        int *temporary = source;\n        source = target;\n        target = temporary;\n    }\n\n    if (source != values)\n        memcpy(values, source, count * sizeof(*values));\n}\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\nstatic void radix_sort_parallel(int *values, int *buffer, size_t count)\n{\n    int maximum_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\n\n    if (maximum_threads <= 1 || count < RADIX_PARALLEL_MIN) {\n        radix_sort_serial(values, buffer, count);\n        return;\n    }\n\n    if ((size_t)maximum_threads > (size_t)-1 / RADIX_BASE) {\n        radix_sort_serial(values, buffer, count);\n        return;\n    }\n\n    size_t slots = (size_t)maximum_threads * RADIX_BASE;\n    size_t *histogram = (size_t *)calloc(slots, sizeof(*histogram));\n    size_t *offsets = (size_t *)malloc(slots * sizeof(*offsets));\n\n    if (histogram == NULL || offsets == NULL) {\n        free(histogram);\n        free(offsets);\n        radix_sort_serial(values, buffer, count);\n        return;\n    }\n\n#pragma omp parallel default(none) shared(values, buffer, count, histogram, offsets)\n    {\n        const int thread_id = omp_get_thread_num();\n        const int thread_count = omp_get_num_threads();\n        const size_t first = count * (size_t)thread_id / (size_t)thread_count;\n        const size_t last = count * (size_t)(thread_id + 1) / (size_t)thread_count;\n        int *source = values;\n        int *target = buffer;\n\n        for (unsigned int shift = 0;\n             shift < sizeof(unsigned int) * CHAR_BIT;\n             shift += 8) {\n            size_t *local_histogram = histogram + (size_t)thread_id * RADIX_BASE;\n\n            for (unsigned int bucket = 0; bucket < RADIX_BASE; bucket++)\n                local_histogram[bucket] = 0;\n\n            for (size_t i = first; i < last; i++) {\n                unsigned int bucket = (radix_key(source[i]) >> shift) & 0xffu;\n                local_histogram[bucket]++;\n            }\n\n#pragma omp barrier\n#pragma omp single\n            {\n                size_t prefix = 0;\n\n                for (unsigned int bucket = 0; bucket < RADIX_BASE; bucket++) {\n                    for (int thread = 0; thread < thread_count; thread++) {\n                        size_t index = (size_t)thread * RADIX_BASE + bucket;\n                        offsets[index] = prefix;\n                        prefix += histogram[index];\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            size_t *local_offsets = offsets + (size_t)thread_id * RADIX_BASE;\n            for (size_t i = first; i < last; i++) {\n                unsigned int bucket = (radix_key(source[i]) >> shift) & 0xffu;\n                target[local_offsets[bucket]++] = source[i];\n            }\n\n#pragma omp barrier\n            int *temporary = source;\n            source = target;\n            target = temporary;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (((sizeof(unsigned int) * CHAR_BIT + 7) / 8) & 1)\n        memcpy(values, buffer, count * sizeof(*values));\n\n    free(offsets);\n    free(histogram);\n}\n#endif\n\n/*\n * A generic pRNG\n */\n#define MY_RAND_MAX 0x7FFFFFFF\n\n#define RANDNUM_W 521288629\n#define RANDNUM_Z 362436069\n\nunsigned int randum_w = RANDNUM_W;\nunsigned int randum_z = RANDNUM_Z;\n\nvoid srandnum(int seed)\n{\n    unsigned int w, z;\n    w = (seed * 104623) & 0xffffffff;\n    randum_w = (w) ? w : RANDNUM_W;\n    z = (seed * 48947) & 0xffffffff;\n    randum_z = (z) ? z : RANDNUM_Z;\n}\n\ndouble randnum(void)\n{\n    unsigned int u;\n    randum_z = 36969 * (randum_z & 65535) + (randum_z >> 16);\n    randum_w = 18000 * (randum_w & 65535) + (randum_w >> 16);\n    u = (randum_z << 16) + randum_w;\n    return (abs(u));\n}\n\n/*\n * Main function\n */\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\n{\n    int N = 0;\n    int *our_list = NULL;\n\n    //The input provides the case size\n    scanf(\"%d\", &N);\n    if (N <= 0) {\n        printf(\"Error: please, provide the case size.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    //Generate the case\n    our_list = generate_case(N);\n    if (our_list == NULL) {\n        printf(\"Error: case instantiation failed.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    //Do the thing\n    quicksort(our_list, N);\n\n    if (is_sorted(our_list, N) == 1) {\n        printf(\"Error, for some reason list is still unsorted.\\n\");\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n#ifdef COMPUTE_MD5_PROBLEM\n    //Compute MD5 Checksum for problem identification\n    MD5_CTX c;\n    unsigned char out[MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH];\n    MD5_Init(&c);\n    MD5_Update(&c, our_list, N * sizeof(int));\n    MD5_Final(out, &c);\n    for (int n = 0; n < MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH; n++) {\n        printf(\"%02x\", out[n]);\n    }\n#endif\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n\n    //Clean up\n    free(our_list);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n\n/*\n * Public API\n */\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N)\n{\n    if (N < 2)\n        return;\n\n    int *buffer = (int *)malloc((size_t)N * sizeof(*buffer));\n    if (buffer == NULL) {\n        _quicksort(toorder, 0, N - 1);\n        return;\n    }\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n    radix_sort_parallel(toorder, buffer, (size_t)N);\n#else\n    radix_sort_serial(toorder, buffer, (size_t)N);\n#endif\n\n    free(buffer);\n}\n\n/*\n * Internal recursive function to quicksort\n */\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    if (lo >= hi)\n        return;\n    int b = partition(toorder, lo, hi);\n    _quicksort(toorder, lo, b - 1);\n    _quicksort(toorder, b + 1, hi);\n}\n\n/*\n * Swap two values.\n */\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j)\n{\n    int temp = toorder[i];\n    toorder[i] = toorder[j];\n    toorder[j] = temp;\n}\n\n/*\n * Partition decision\n */\nint partition(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\n{\n    int b = lo;\n    int r = (int) (lo + (hi - lo) * (randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX));\n    int pivot = toorder[r];\n    swap(toorder, r, hi);\n    for (int i = lo; i < hi; i++) {\n        if (toorder[i] < pivot) {\n            swap(toorder, i, b);\n            b++;\n        }\n    }\n    swap(toorder, hi, b);\n    return b;\n}\n\n/*\n * Check if elements are in non-decreasing order\n */\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N)\n{\n    for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {\n        if (toorder[i] < toorder[i - 1]) {\n            return 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\n\n/*\n * Generate a case\n */\nint *generate_case(int N)\n{\n    int i;\n    int *ret = NULL;\n\n    // Make case generation reproducible\n    srandnum(0);\n\n    // Allocate memory\n    ret = (int *) malloc((size_t)N * sizeof(*ret));\n    if (ret == NULL) {\n        printf(\"Error: some malloc won't work.\\n\");\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    // Get pseudo-random positive integer values\n    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        ret[i] = drand(0, INT_MAX);\n    }\n    return ret;\n}\n\n/*\n * A pseudo-random number between two positive integer values\n */\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax)\n{\n    return xmin + (xmax - xmin) * randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX;\n}\n","path":"src/quicksort.c"}],"hypothesis":"A stable four-pass signed-integer radix sort eliminates comparison-heavy recursive quicksort work; for sufficiently large arrays, one persistent OpenMP team with deterministic contiguous chunks, per-thread histograms, and a single prefix reduction improves four-core throughput while preserving exact sorted bytes.","notes":"Uses a serial radix fallback for small arrays, unavailable OpenMP support, and temporary-allocation failures; the original quicksort remains the final allocation-failure fallback.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace the primary comparison sort with stable LSD radix sorting over all unsigned-int bytes, using a sign-bit transform so the public sorter retains signed integer ordering.","For large arrays under OpenMP, perform each radix pass in one persistent team: disjoint contiguous histogram/scatter ranges, cache-line-separated per-thread rows, and a deterministic single-thread prefix reduction.","Retain low-overhead serial radix behavior for small arrays and portable non-OpenMP builds, with the original quicksort as an allocation-failure fallback."]}